CNet PRO BBS 3.0 system HELP utility: HELP MENU

At most command prompts (>), entering a question mark (?) will display a summary of all available commands.  Another command, Quit, is also handy to know to get back to the Main> prompt.

The purpose of this help utility is to explain some of the more complicated commands and features of the CNet BBS system.

To abort this or any message, press the SPACEBAR.  Hold down the CONTROL key and press S to pause the text display, and then any other key to resume.

The Help utility is available from all command prompts. HELP <TOPICNAME> is also an acceptable way to get help from the help utility.

Press the ENTER key to return to the command prompt.  Enter LIST for a complete list of all available help keywords.  The following list shows some commonly asked about topics:

